{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Sign","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","text":"Sign"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStaffLinePositionV","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"octaveChange"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLOctaveChangeV","text":"MXLOctaveChange"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sign element represents the clef symbol."}]}],"name":"sign"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Line numbers are counted from the bottom of the staff. They are only needed with the G, F, and C signs in order to position a pitch correctly on the staff. Standard values are 2 for the G sign (treble clef), 4 for the F sign (bass clef), and 3 for the C sign (alto clef). Line values can be used to specify positions outside the staff, such as a C clef positioned in the middle of a grand staff."}]}],"name":"line"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clef-octave-change element is used for transposing clefs. A treble clef for tenors would have a value of -1."}]}],"name":"octaveChange"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLClef.Content"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","text":"Sign"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStaffLinePositionV","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"octaveChange"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLOctaveChangeV","text":"MXLOctaveChange"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"title":"init(sign:line:octaveChange:)","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Initializer","symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV7ContentV4sign4line12octaveChangeAeC4SignO_AA20MXLStaffLinePositionVSgAA09MXLOctaveH0VSgtcfc"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octavechange:)"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octaveChange:)"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveChange":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveChange","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLOctaveChange","abstract":[{"text":"The number of octaves to shift a pitch or clef, such as when transposing a written pitch to a sounding pitch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the octave-change element) or positioning a treble clef for tenors, which would use a value of -1 (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clef-octave-change element).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctavechange"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef":{"title":"MXLClef","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements. The optional number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute refers to staff numbers within the part. A value of 1 is assumed if not present."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Content-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct","type":"topic","title":"MXLClef.Content","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/content-swift.struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Sign":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/sign","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Sign"}],"title":"MXLClef.Sign","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clef-sign type represents the different clef symbols. The jianpu sign indicates that the music that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows should be in jianpu numbered notation, just as the TAB sign indicates that the music that follows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be in tablature notation. Unlike TAB, a jianpu sign does not correspond to a visual clef notation."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Sign"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Sign"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Content-swift.struct/init(sign:line:octaveChange:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octavechange:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sign"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStaffLinePositionV","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"octaveChange","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLOctaveChangeV","text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(sign:line:octaveChange:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLClef.Content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octaveChange:)","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffLinePosition":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffLinePosition","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-line-position type indicates the line position on a given staff. Staff lines are numbered from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"bottom to top, with 1 being the bottom line on a staff. A staff-line-position value can extend beyond the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"range of the lines on the current staff.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstafflineposition","title":"MXLStaffLinePosition"}}}